{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012gREYrhkUvXvmUws1q6b32","type":"tool_result","content":"# smoke tier); the coverage step runs several times longer. These are snapshots,\n# not contracts — re-measure locally before budgeting against them (the prior\n# ~65 s figure predated the v4 dispatch/integrate suite growth and misled\n# session budgeting for weeks; repo-review 2026-07-21 M-24).\n# The `smoke` tier stays as declared; the coverage args below still apply.\ntest = {py} -m pytest -q -n auto\n\n[tiers]\nsmoke = -m smoke\nfull = -m \"not release\"\nrelease =\nall =\n--\n[smoke-budget]\n# WI-281: the per-commit smoke bar ([tiers] smoke, run by the session-protocol\n# commit bar) must stay a real smoke test — \"is it basically alive?\" — not a\n# re-run of the full suite. WI-122's opt-out default had inverted: 1088/1378\n# (79%) of tests ran per commit at ~6 min wall. The budget is SPLIT in two,\n# because a wall-clock assert is machine-/core-count-dependent and flaky:\n--\n===\n# AGENTS.md\n\nThe contributor guide for **this meta-repo** is [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md) — read\nit first. It governs editing the reusable kit in\n[`project-trajectory/`](project-trajectory/). This stub exists so agents that\nread `AGENTS.md` (Codex and others) land on that guide too; the content lives in\n`CLAUDE.md`, not here.\n\n> Note: the kit *ships* the inverse convention — downstream projects get a full\n> `AGENTS.md` with `CLAUDE.md`/`GEMINI.md` stubs. Here `CLAUDE.md` is the home\n> because that's the historical guide for this repo; this `AGENTS.md` dogfoods\n> the cross-tool pointer pattern.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80264356-be81-4c4a-a091-63cf3e079d5f","uuid":"c606ab45-5d65-4e82-9cfd-76d7162033db","timestamp":"2026-09-01T04:44:41.078Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# smoke tier); the coverage step runs several times longer. These are snapshots,\n# not contracts — re-measure locally before budgeting against the